  "root_causes_fixed": ["Baseline combat averaged 60.25 props/update, 45.91 wholly redundant. Minimap navigation alone averaged 1.47 ms, 1,889 allocations and 37.65 messages every frame. Conditional movement/styles remove the repeated work before Shoes serialization.", "ObjectSpace found 216 arrays and 36 hashes per warmed fixture frame from reconstructing each grub animation table, plus paths, name/HP strings and position arrays. Immutable animation/path constants and retained actor data remove this churn.", "Outlined names require five paragraphs; newly revealed names are now limited to two per frame instead of eight. Hidden actors defer zoom geometry except the active actor, whose bounds must remain correct for aim markers.", "The lock pulse, flame rate, sprite poses and aim geometry are preserved. Only rounded visual changes send messages; offscreen hazards retain simulation state while deferring image changes until visible.", "Terrain and minimap swaps were measured but were not the dominant recurring Ruby cost; no worker or terrain protocol restructuring was justified."],
  "gc_decision": "No launcher heap settings, disabled runtime GC or forced idle collections. Allocation reductions reduce collection pressure; diagnosed long stalls had zero GC. Mac Ruby 3.4.7 heap/RSS and pause measurements are needed before changing packaged GC policy.",
