  "suggestions_for_other_owners": {
    "timeline.rb": "~632 allocations/sample and 0.27 ms mean CPU remain, accounting for much of the optimized idle/pan allocation rate. Reuse interpolation scratch storage and avoid per-worm merge/zip/to_h while preserving elapsed time, short flights and pruned-history recovery.",
    "connection.rb": "Measure decode/receive and GVL waits on the actual Mac build before a protocol redesign. Decode averages ~0.65 ms CPU, peaks ~4-5 ms in these profiled captures. Keep socket work off the GUI thread.",
    "vendor/scarpe and patches/scarpe": "Large zooms still emit hundreds of required geometry/text updates (up to 545/update in this final live capture). A native text outline could replace five paragraph nodes per name; cheaper native props/layout/image-cache handling would address the remaining burst. Upstream unchanged-value filtering would protect other callers, but avoiding Ruby setters still saves serialization and allocations.",
    "audio.rb": "Re-test audible event timing after integration on the M3 Pro. Linux OpenAL null mixing is not evidence of audible Mac output."
